`{{.Binary}}`: {{.Description}}.

# What It Does

- **Status checks:** Reports runtime readiness and the installed version with `{{.Binary}} status`.
- **Agent output:** Prints compact, machine-readable output when `AGENT=1` is set.
- **Agent skill:** Publishes a complete command and option guide that `{{.Binary}} skill` tells you how to install.
- **Command tree help:** Shows every command and its subcommands in one wrapped, aligned help screen.

# How It Works

- Run `{{.Binary}} --help` to see the available commands.
- Run a command such as `{{.Binary}} status` to get its result on stdout.
- Set `AGENT=1` to switch every command to compact agent output.

# How it Really Works

- Values `1`, `true`, and `yes` for `AGENT` enable agent output, with case and surrounding whitespace ignored. Any other value keeps human output.
- Help text wraps to the terminal width and is never cut off.
- Results go to stdout, errors go to stderr, and failures exit with status 1.
- `{{.Binary}} skill` works offline. The guide itself is published at [`skills/{{.Binary}}`](skills/{{.Binary}}/SKILL.md) in this repository, not bundled in the binary.

# Installation

Download the prebuilt binary for your platform from the [latest release](https://github.com/{{.Repository}}/releases/latest), replacing `X.X.X` with the version shown on that page.

```bash
# macOS (Apple Silicon)
curl -sSL https://github.com/{{.Repository}}/releases/latest/download/{{.Binary}}_X.X.X_darwin_arm64.tar.gz | tar -xz -C ~/.local/bin
```

# Quick Start

```bash
# Show help and available commands
{{.Binary}} --help

# Check binary version
{{.Binary}} --version

# Run status check
{{.Binary}} status

# Show how to install the agent skill
{{.Binary}} skill
```

Sample Output:

```text
$ {{.Binary}} status
[OK] System status: ready
Version: 0.1.0
```

# Options & Flags

| Flag | Short | Default | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `--help` | `-h` | `false` | Display help and command tree |
| `--version` | `-v` | `false` | Display binary version |

